    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear offensive ceiling, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (81.26) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play, capitalizing on a massive favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (17.18 xERA); the combination of an elite hitter in a high-run environment makes him our undisputed cornerstone. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits significantly from the matchup against Young, whose 4.77 xERA provides a soft landing for a hitter currently riding high on dynamic platoon splits. **Josh Lowe** (71.68) and **Andy Pages** (70.87) also offer strong value, with **Josh Lowe** in particular seeing his efficiency climb due to his positive interaction with the Sasaki matchup, proving that our outfield depth is the engine of the squad today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 56.80 score, just missing the cut for the final utility slot. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from a platoon edge against Lovelady, his lower base projection relative to **Dominic Smith** (56.83) ultimately relegated him to the bench; **Dominic Smith**\u2019s slight efficiency edge against Bello makes him the statistically safer play for today\u2019s rotation. We remain mindful of the risks posed by **Gunnar Henderson** (61.92), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon differential against Lovelady, requiring him to rely more on raw talent than favorable context to hit his projected floor.\n\nOur focus on speed remains a strategic imperative, yet we have opted to sit **Miguel Vargas** (52.02) despite his 63% SB hold rate, as his current efficiency metrics don't justify a start over the higher-scoring options like **Sam Antonacci** (61.39). **Sam Antonacci** is a key watch item today; his elite xwOBA of 0.400, combined with a lead-off spot against Rea, provides the exact type of category-stabilizing production we need. As we manage our game caps, we are keeping **Jackson Merrill** (51.78) and **Josh Jung** (49.71) in reserve, as their matchup difficulty against Kirby and Lambert, respectively, limits their utility when compared to the higher-ceiling profiles of **Nolan Schanuel** (62.47) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.93).",
